---
layout: base.njk
title: Sources & Methodology — Admizz Group
description: Every third-party statistic and Admizz-published figure cited on this site, indexed with its primary source.
permalink: /sources/
---

{# /sources/ — rebuilt 2026-09-08 v2.

   v1 was a hand-written <ul><li> list, left-aligned inside the 95vw shell
   (measured: 645px of content, 1,149px of empty page beside it). Two
   problems beyond the layout: the figures that are the entire point of
   the page were buried mid-sentence inside list items, and the three very
   different kinds of proof it carries all looked identical.

   Now assembled from src/_data/citations.js, which reads marketContext /
   universities / destinations directly — so this page and the counts on
   it cannot drift from what the site actually cites, and a new citation
   only has to be added in one place.

   The tiers stay structurally separate because that separation is the
   page's argument: independently verifiable research, the one verified
   credential, and Admizz's own published figures — the last clearly
   marked as self-reported rather than quietly mixed in with the rest. #}

<section class="bg-paper py-section-sm">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="page-canvas">
      <span class="eyebrow" data-hero-in>Methodology</span>
      <h1 class="mt-3 font-display font-light text-display-2 text-ink max-w-[22ch] text-balance" data-hero-in>Where our numbers come from.</h1>
      <p class="mt-5 text-body-lg text-ink-muted max-w-measure" data-hero-in>
        Every statistic on this site is sourced. Third-party research is independently verifiable at the link given &mdash; we read the primary source directly before publishing a figure, never a search summary or a secondhand citation.
      </p>

      <div class="bento mt-12 md:mt-16">
        <div class="bento-item fade-up">
          <span class="font-mono text-label uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-faint">Citations on this site</span>
          <div>
            <p class="bento-num font-display font-light tabular-nums text-ink">{{ citations.counts.total }}</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-small text-ink-muted">Every figure below is traceable to a named source.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="bento-item bento-item-navy fade-up" style="animation-delay:80ms">
          <span class="font-mono text-label uppercase tracking-widest text-navy-accent">Independently verifiable</span>
          <div>
            <p class="bento-num font-display font-light tabular-nums text-navy-on">{{ citations.counts.independent }}</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-small text-navy-on-muted">Third-party research and government data, each linked to its primary source.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="bento-item bento-item-tint fade-up" style="animation-delay:160ms">
          <span class="font-mono text-label uppercase tracking-widest text-gold-text">Publishers</span>
          <div>
            <p class="bento-num font-display font-light tabular-nums text-ink">{{ citations.counts.publishers }}</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-small text-ink-muted">Pearson, College Board, IIE, NAFSA, federal statistics agencies and others.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="bento-item fade-up" style="animation-delay:240ms">
          <span class="font-mono text-label uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-faint">Fabricated</span>
          <div>
            <p class="bento-num font-display font-light tabular-nums text-ink">0</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-small text-ink-muted">Where a figure doesn&rsquo;t exist yet, this site says so rather than filling the gap.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{# ---------- Tier 1: independent research ---------- #}
<section class="bg-paper pb-section">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="page-canvas">

      <div class="source-tier fade-up">
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline justify-between gap-3">
          <h2 class="font-display font-book text-h3 text-ink">Independent third-party research</h2>
          <span class="font-mono text-label uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-faint">{{ citations.counts.independent }} citations &middot; {{ citations.counts.publishers }} publishers</span>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-2 text-body text-ink-muted max-w-measure">
          Sector and market data describing the industries our ventures operate in &mdash; not claims about Admizz itself. Cited on <a href="/ventures/" class="link-underline text-ink">/ventures/</a> and across our research articles.
        </p>

        <div class="mt-8">
          {% for c in citations.independent %}
          <div class="source-row">
            <p class="source-figure font-display font-light text-ink">
              {% if c.value %}{{ c.value }}{% else %}<span class="source-figure-none font-sans">Context</span>{% endif %}
            </p>
            <div>
              <p class="text-body text-ink leading-relaxed">{{ c.label }}</p>
              <p class="mt-1.5 font-mono text-label uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-faint">{{ c.venture }}</p>
            </div>
            <a href="{{ c.href }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="source-publisher text-small font-medium text-ink link-underline">
              {{ c.publisher }}
              <svg width="11" height="11" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" class="shrink-0"><path d="M4 10L10 4M10 4H5.5M10 4v4.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
            </a>
          </div>
          {% endfor %}
        </div>
      </div>

      {# ---------- Tier 2: accreditation ---------- #}
      <div class="source-tier mt-6 fade-up">
        <h2 class="font-display font-book text-h3 text-ink">Accreditation</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-body text-ink-muted max-w-measure">
          Verifiable directly through ICEF&rsquo;s own agency directory &mdash; not self-reported.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-8">
          {% for c in citations.accreditation %}
          <div class="source-row">
            <p class="source-figure font-display font-light text-ink">{{ c.value }}</p>
            <div>
              <p class="text-body text-ink leading-relaxed">{{ c.label }}</p>
              <p class="mt-1.5 font-mono text-label uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-faint">{{ c.venture }}</p>
            </div>
            <a href="{{ c.href }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="source-publisher text-small font-medium text-ink link-underline">
              Verify with {{ c.publisher }}
              <svg width="11" height="11" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" class="shrink-0"><path d="M4 10L10 4M10 4H5.5M10 4v4.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
            </a>
          </div>
          {% endfor %}
        </div>
      </div>

      {# ---------- Tier 3: self-reported ---------- #}
      <div class="source-tier source-tier-flag mt-6 fade-up">
        <h2 class="font-display font-book text-h3 text-ink">Admizz&rsquo;s own published figures</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-body text-ink-muted max-w-measure">
          Real and attributed, but self-reported rather than independently audited. We cite them as Admizz Education&rsquo;s own stated results &mdash; never as third-party fact &mdash; and label them that way wherever they appear.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-8">
          {% for c in citations.selfReported %}
          <div class="source-row">
            <p class="source-figure font-display font-light text-ink">
              {% if c.value %}{{ c.value }}{% else %}<span class="source-figure-none font-sans">Various</span>{% endif %}
            </p>
            <div>
              <p class="text-body text-ink leading-relaxed">{{ c.label }}</p>
              <p class="mt-1.5 font-mono text-label uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-faint">{{ c.venture }}</p>
            </div>
            <span class="text-small text-ink-muted">{{ c.publisher }}</span>
          </div>
          {% endfor %}
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-14 max-w-measure fade-up">
        <h2 class="font-display font-book text-h3 text-ink">What we don&rsquo;t do</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-body text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">
          We don&rsquo;t cite a figure we haven&rsquo;t read at its primary source, and we don&rsquo;t publish a statistic we can&rsquo;t attribute. Where real information doesn&rsquo;t yet exist for something this site could otherwise show &mdash; a metric, a case study, a named team member &mdash; we say so plainly rather than filling the gap with an invented number. If you find a citation here that&rsquo;s gone stale or broken, we&rsquo;d want to know: <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}" class="link-underline text-ink">{{ site.email }}</a>.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{% include "partials/cta-close.njk" %}
